  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is positive (≥0.00) and model shows persistent overestimation.",
    "Reduce forecast peaks by 5-10% after a spike if sentiment is neutral or negative (≤0.00) to avoid overshoot.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if 3 consecutive forecast days are above 70.00, reduce by 1-2% per day unless sentiment strongly supports.",
    "If sentiment increases (e.g., >0.00) after a low, slightly increase forecast to reflect momentum, but cap at +5% above recent 7-day average.",
    "For 30-day forecasts, if true outcome deviates >3% from 14-day moving average, adjust forecast to align with recent trend, not just historical mean."
  ]
}
